# Three client suites (`farm`, `town`, `engine-agreement`) load the cage module through Node's own
# `require`, because that is what proves the client and the cages resolve to one module and one data
# file. That module is TypeScript, so Node has to strip types — automatic only from 22.18 up, and on an
# older runtime the three suites fail to *load* while the run still reports 46 passing files.
#
# `NODE_OPTIONS` and not a CLI flag on the script: vitest runs each suite in a worker, and a worker
# inherits the environment but not the parent's command-line flags. This is the same flag every
# `tools/*.ts` script in the root package.json already passes.
node-options=--experimental-strip-types --disable-warning=ExperimentalWarning
